{{!--
    Primary and secondary navigation, with one level of dropdown.

    Ghost's navigation is a flat list, so nesting is a convention: an item whose
    label starts with "- " becomes a child of the item above it.

        Home                →  top level, links to /
        - With sidebar      →  child of Home
        - Without sidebar   →  child of Home
        About               →  top level again

    A publisher sets this up entirely in Settings → Navigation; there is nothing
    to configure in the theme.

    ── Why the markup is written this way ──────────────────────────────────────

    Handlebars cannot look ahead, so the template cannot ask "does a child
    follow?" before deciding whether to open a panel. Instead every top-level
    item opens a panel unconditionally, and the panel is closed by the *next*
    top-level item — or after the loop. That balances the tags without any
    lookahead, and CSS hides the panels that turn out to be empty with
    :empty.

    The parent stays a real link. The panel opens on hover and on focus-within,
    so it works with a keyboard and needs no JavaScript at all.

    The child's own label is printed through {{split}}, which drops empty parts —
    so "- With sidebar" split on "- " yields just "With sidebar" and the marker
    never reaches the page. Ghost has no string-replace helper; this is the way
    to do it with what it ships.

    ── {{this.url}}, not {{url}} ───────────────────────────────────────────────

    Ghost registers `url` as a helper, and a helper wins over a context property
    of the same name. Writing {{url}} inside this loop calls the helper and
    returns the *current page's* URL, so every item in the menu links to the same
    place — with no error anywhere to say so. The explicit `this.` is what makes
    it read the navigation item's own url.

    Parameters
      variant   header | drawer | footer
      type      primary (default) | secondary
      label     accessible name for the <nav> landmark
--}}
<nav class="ghost-nav ghost-nav--{{variant}}" aria-label="{{label}}">
    <ul class="ghost-nav__list">
        {{#match type "secondary"}}

            {{#foreach @site.secondary_navigation}}
                <li class="ghost-nav__item">
                    <a class="ghost-nav__link{{link_class for=this.url activeClass=" ghost-nav__link--current"}}" href="{{this.url}}">{{label}}</a>
                </li>
            {{/foreach}}

        {{else}}

            {{#foreach @site.navigation}}
                {{#match label "~^" "- "}}
                    {{!-- A child. It lands inside the panel the previous
                         top-level item left open. --}}
                    <li class="ghost-nav__sub-item">
                        <a class="ghost-nav__sub-link{{link_class for=this.url activeClass=" ghost-nav__sub-link--current"}}" href="{{this.url}}">{{split label separator="- "}}</a>
                    </li>
                {{else}}
                    {{!-- A top level item. Close the previous one's panel first,
                         unless this is the first item and nothing is open. --}}
                    {{#unless @first}}</ul></li>{{/unless}}
                    <li class="ghost-nav__item">
                        <a class="ghost-nav__link{{link_class for=this.url activeClass=" ghost-nav__link--current"}}" href="{{this.url}}">
                            {{label}}
                            <span class="ghost-nav__chevron" aria-hidden="true">{{> "icon" name="chevron-down"}}</span>
                        </a>
                        <ul class="ghost-nav__panel">
                {{/match}}
            {{/foreach}}

            {{!-- Close the last item's panel. --}}
            {{#if @site.navigation}}</ul></li>{{/if}}

        {{/match}}
    </ul>
</nav>
